# THE NAMES, NEVER THE VALUES. Plan task 5a-iii-a.
#
# Copy to `app/.env.local` and fill in from the Supabase dashboard
# (Project Settings → API, or the Connect dialog). `.env.local` is gitignored
# by `app/.gitignore` (`.env*.local`); this file is the committed record of
# what the app reads, so a fresh clone fails with a name it can look up rather
# than with `undefined`.
#
# ⚠️ THE PREFIX IS `EXPO_PUBLIC_`, NOT `NEXT_PUBLIC_`. Supabase's Connect
# dialog has a framework picker and hands out the Next.js spelling by default —
# the owner pasted exactly that on 2026-09-11. Expo inlines ONLY
# `EXPO_PUBLIC_`-prefixed variables, so the Next spelling is not a wrong value,
# it is NO value: `undefined`, and nothing in the app can tell the difference
# between that and a variable nobody set. `docs/checks/5a-iii-gate.sh` reads
# this file's real sibling and is the only instrument that can see the trap.
#
# ⚠️ THE KEY IS THE PUBLISHABLE ONE (`sb_publishable_…`), AND IT IS NOT A
# SECRET. It is designed to ship inside the app binary; anyone holding the app
# holds it, and RLS is what protects the data. Its counterpart — `sb_secret_…`
# / `service_role` — BYPASSES RLS ENTIRELY and must never appear in a file the
# client reads. `app/src/lib/env.ts` refuses to build a client with one, and
# `app/test/env.test.ts` is what keeps that refusal true.
#
# ⚠️ INLINED AT BUILD TIME, NOT READ AT RUNTIME. After editing `.env.local`,
# restart the dev server — `npx expo start --clear` if it does not pick it up.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
